  "observations": {
    "bitmap": "Normal DIB wrapper1ad030 chooses requested internal enum1 for24bit or2 otherwise; when texture+0x8c is set it chooses0x32 for24bit or0x35 otherwise (instruction immediates at1ad226/1ad22b). Those map to DXT1 RGB0x83f0 / DXT5 RGBA0x83f3 when global compression support1415c2ad3 is enabled, otherwise ordinary RGB0x1907 / RGBA0x1908. It always passes raw external enum3 for24bit or4 otherwise, sampleType0x1401. Thus normal bitmap pixels enter ordinary glTexImage2D, not the precompressed DXT byte-buffer path.",
    "channels": "enum3 maps GL_BGR0x80e0; enum4 maps GL_BGRA0x80e1. Internal enum1/3 maps RGB8 0x8051, enum2/4 maps RGBA8 0x8058. Generic compressed storage requests0x30/0x31 also exist, mapping0x84ed/0x84ee, but are NOT the DIB wrapper selection. Its compression flag selects0x32/0x35 while retaining ordinary BGR/BGRA input. Exact compressed output is driver-dependent/unmeasured.",
    "storage": "Helper1ac520 is storage units: bytes per represented pixel for ordinary enum families, bytes per4x4 block for enabled S3TC0x32..0x35. It is not a universal channel count. Preserve original anomalous family values; do not normalize by guessed names.",
    "allocation": "Raw1aca70 rejects only null pixels or texture name0 before binding. Unsigned width>=storedWidth AND height>=storedHeight chooses allocation; either smaller chooses subimage at level0/offset0. Equal sizes allocate. DIB wrapper stores current dimensions before calling, therefore selects allocation on its normal path.",
    "compressed": "Only external enum0x32..0x35 plus global1415c2ad3 use compressed image/subimage function pointers. Byte count is unchecked uint32(storage*((width+3)>>2)*((height+3)>>2)); widths+3 wrap before shift. Missing compressed upload function pointer skips upload but still follows cleanup and returns true. Never equate original boolean success with actual GPU output.",
